J6inmCbKMh", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19854, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JkDTUunJDtinJ6inmCbKMh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25509, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011jeTAY8jcep13wsnjToaZb", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api started failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed. The error rate was 18% in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both marked unhealthy. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which briefly left regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56109, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011jeTAY8jcep13wsnjToaZb", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56109, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011jeTAY8jcep13wsnjToaZb", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58891, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017pnZPKU62fg9dJDvAGv2AV", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59191, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017pnZPKU62fg9dJDvAGv2AV", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59191, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017pnZPKU62fg9dJDvAGv2AV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64379, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 was failing in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once, and that finished us-west and eu-west.\n- The service now shows all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2% (0.002).\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list so the on-call engineer wouldn't be paged twice. It had been created as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open).\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and the retry) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 problem, and looking into the orchestrator error during the rollback.\n\nNo change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CziskcmcXfU2mGSC8527t9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "too