briefly left regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may have been created anyway. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017pnZPKU62fg9dJDvAGv2AV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.1 was failing in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also marked unhealthy, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once, and that finished us-west and eu-west.\n- The service now shows all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2% (0.002).\n\n**Incident:**\n- The request to open the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list so the on-call engineer wouldn't be paged twice. It had been created as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open).\n- The incident describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and the retry) and the current state. It lists two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 problem, and looking into the orchestrator error during the rollback.\n\nNo change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}